 "notes": [
  "One model only (Autodesk sample), three storeys: a smoke test of the masking step, not a result about generalisation. One seed.",
  "Folds by storey: the test storey's doors and windows never enter training, not even as context.",
  "One element hidden at a time, the rest of its subgraph visible (\"one by one\"); its level is given.",
  "The host is always inside the subgraph (E1: 100%), so the host is picked among the piece's walls (about 15).",
  "Placement sits on the predicted wall line; the sill comes from the predicted type (median of training).",
  "Copy baseline: the nearest door or window of the training storeys, projected onto a candidate wall. within_10cm_of_a_training_floor_opening_pct measures how much of each answer could be a copy from another floor; truth_within_10cm_... is the same measure on the real model (stacked openings).",
  "The place along the wall is not learned: with the right host the median error (position_error_when_host_right_m) is about the same as putting every element at the middle of its true wall (reference_middle_of_true_host_m). Class, type and host are learned; the place is not.",
  "No element lands within 1 cm, so the 1 cm check of E3 will place none of them exactly; E3 has to judge by host and type, and by distance bands.",
  "Settings (80 epochs, 3 layers, d=64) were fixed before the run and not tuned on the test storeys.",
  "Not tested: hiding all openings of a piece at once, walls or rooms, hand/facing flip, and more than one model."
